From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] make_specfiles: child spec files follow their parents again (5908)

tools/make_specfiles keeps the spec files of DLLs that share an
implementation in step; the drafters changed the parent specs (bcrypt,
msvcrt, msvcp, d3dx10_43, sppc, secur32, srvsvc, bthprops, mscoree) without
running it, so the children kept "stub" entries for functions their parent
now implements, or forwards. This is the tool's output, no hand edits:
- ncrypt, cng.sys: the BCrypt context/provider functions forward to bcrypt;
- msvcrt20, msvcrt40, msvcr120_app, msvcp60/100/110/120/120_app/140/_win:
  the C/C++ runtime entries of their parents;
- d3dx10_33 .. d3dx10_42: d3dx10_43's;
- slc (sppc), sspicli (secur32), srvcli (srvsvc), irprops.cpl (bthprops),
  mscorwks (mscoree).

Coordinator decision (integ-2026-10): child specs out of sync with their
parents are a merge artifact. Conformance suites of these DLLs in stage D.
